-- title:
--   Weight-one Tate model and cusp points over K
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, equipped with a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$; write $\xi_u$ for $\xi$ viewed as a unit of $L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $\Gamma_H$ with $H =$ `levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, at level $(q\ell)^2M'$. Then there is a Weierstrass variable change $C=\langle u,r,s,t\rangle$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with $r$, $s$, $t$ the constant Laurent series $-1/12$, $-1/2$, $1/24$, with $u$ satisfying $u\,(2x_P + 1/6) = 2y_P + x_P$ where $(x_P,y_P) =$ `cuspPoint` $L\,(q\ell)\,\xi_u\,(1,0)$ (the toric Tate point at $c=\xi$), such that all five coefficients $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6$ of $C \bullet$ `tateBase` $L\,(q\ell)$ — the formal Tate curve over Laurent series in $L$ with $q$ replaced by $q^{q\ell}$ — lie in $K$, and such that for all nonzero $v,w \in (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^2$ the coordinates $x_P,y_P$ of the $C$-transform of `cuspData` $L\,(q\ell)\,\xi_u\,v\,w$, namely $u^{-2}(x_P-r)$ and $u^{-3}(y_P-s(x_P-r)-t)$ for $(x_P,y_P)$ the cusp point attached to $v$, lie in $K$. Since only the $P$-coordinates are asserted, the conclusion depends on $v$ alone, $w$ being immaterial.
--
--   This is the statement that, after the weight-one change of variables with $r=-1/12$, $s=-1/2$, $t=1/24$ and $u$ normalised by the toric cusp point at index $(1,0)$, the Tate curve at parameter $q^{q\ell}$ and the coordinates of its cusp torsion points are rational over the compositum $K$ of $L$ with the modular function field of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_variableChange_tateBase_mem_laurentBaseChange_and_cuspData_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_variableChange_tateBase_mem_laurentBaseChange_and_cuspData_mem), where the resulting model over $K$ carries the level structure.
